#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/unit-questions-and-answers.adoc:214
#, no-wrap
msgid "Can you explain how to avoid splitting a combat when casting Raise Dead?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/unit-questions-and-answers.adoc:218
msgid ""
"Yes. Take this starting combat, where you want to raise a unit of Skeletons. "
"The arrows indicate in which direction the red and orange units are fighting "
"and supporting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/unit-questions-and-answers.adoc:223
msgid ""
"You are not allowed to raise the unit as shown in <<raise-dead-2>>, as the "
"red and orange units are now fighting two separate combats."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/unit-questions-and-answers.adoc:228
msgid ""
"Instead, you can Raise Dead as per <<raise-dead-3>> or <<raise-dead-4>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/unit-questions-and-answers.adoc:237
msgid ""
"In <<raise-dead-3>>, the rightmost orange unit still supports the red unit, "
"keeping the combat as a single combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/unit-questions-and-answers.adoc:240
msgid ""
"In <<raise-dead-4>>, the flanking stand of Raised Dead touches both red and "
"orange units, linking them into one combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/unit-questions-and-answers.adoc:247
msgid ""
"By placing the Raised Dead in this manner you are avoiding splitting the "
"combat while still blocking the retreat of the enemy units. Since each unit "
"must retreat away from the most enemy stands in contact, this will mean the "
"red and orange units will retreat in different directions. The retreating "
"units will block each other’s escapes, as the rear unit will retreat “down” "
"and the front unit will retreat “up”.  But both units will find their "
"retreat blocked by a friendly unit that is in combat and the unit that moves "
"first will be destroyed as there is no room to retreat!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/unit-questions-and-answers.adoc:250
msgid ""
"With the first unit destroyed, the second unit will then have a 2cm space to "
"retreat into… but if they need to move further, they will likely contact "
